# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in. Nothing in this file may carry
# a real host, address or port: `web/` is mirrored to a public repository.

# --- development only --------------------------------------------------------
#
# Where `npm run dev` proxies `/v1`. The account pages need the API to be
# same-origin, because the session is an HttpOnly cookie and the API sends no
# CORS headers; the dev-server proxy is what makes that true on localhost.
#
# The dev API is bound to loopback on its own host, so the usual value here is
# the near end of an SSH tunnel:
#
#     ssh -N -L <port>:127.0.0.1:<port> <user>@<host>
#
# Addresses and ports are in `infra/`, which is not published.
META_API_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:<port>

# --- build time --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Where the browser should send API calls. Leave unset: the default is `/v1`,
# relative, which is the only shape that works with the session cookie until the
# API is served from the same origin as this site. Set it only alongside a CORS
# policy on the API that names this origin and allows credentials.
#
# VITE_META_API_BASE=/v1
